fix: remove control entities when writes are unavailable

The control platforms create nothing when there is no client to drive them
-- control actions switched off, or an API key, which cannot write at all.
Whatever they created on an earlier run stayed in the entity registry, so
Home Assistant kept showing a permanently unavailable row for each button
and for the fan selector. That reads as a fault rather than as a setting
the user chose.

Setup now clears those rows, keyed on the same condition the platforms
use, so the registry cannot disagree with what they create. Which
platforms are control-only is stated once, in const.

Measured before the change: turning controls off left all five entities
in the registry, every one of them unavailable.
